<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heeren XVII</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Heeren XVII, or Seventeen Lords, was the governing board of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>, composed of delegates from its regional chambers. It set policy for the company's trade, fleets and overseas posts. It was a central institution in the governance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heeren-xvii.jpg" alt="Heeren XVII" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Himasaram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Dutch_East_India_Company.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
